      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall this LGTM, but I just wanted to check if we should consider introducing a TraceReferencesWrapper in prebuilts/r8?\n\nThe TraceReferences CLI is somewhat limited in what it can do, since it is not possible to pass a custom consumer. If we want to make it easy to use TraceReferences for other things I could see an advantage to having the wrapper, since that would allow implementing custom consumers, which could be used to implement various checks on the generated dex, such as no `jspecify` references (in the context of b/398249876), or more generally, no references outside a given allowlist for builds that go on the bootclasspath.",
      "revId": "f47c00fdb410bfe05167aac7ae50850bf5b759dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
